Require SSL configuration value types before accepting SSL_CONF commands.
Vesk exposes SSL_CONF_FLAG_FILE but does not implement SSL_CONF_cmd.
Use nginx's existing rejection path when the required API is unavailable.

--- a/src/event/ngx_event_openssl.c
+++ b/src/event/ngx_event_openssl.c
@@ -1880 +1880,2 @@ ngx_ssl_conf_commands(ngx_conf_t *cf, ngx_ssl_t *ssl, ngx_array_t *commands)
-#ifdef SSL_CONF_FLAG_FILE
+#if defined(SSL_CONF_FLAG_FILE) && defined(SSL_CONF_TYPE_FILE)                 \
+    && defined(SSL_CONF_TYPE_DIR)
